# ai-standards per-repo config — coverage scope for the local pre-push gate.
#
# jackui is a media server: most packages drive live I/O (torrent streaming,
# ffmpeg transcoding, HTTP handlers, torrent/HTTP RPC, mailer SMTP). Those can't
# reach 90% unit coverage and aren't meant to — CI races the WHOLE module for
# correctness (`go test ./... -race`) and SonarCloud enforces the real quality
# gate (it already excludes live-I/O from coverage). This file makes the local
# pre-push gate match that reality: the ≥90% floor applies ONLY to the pure-logic
# packages below (the same ones that are already at/above 90%), so the gate stops
# blocking every push on packages that are excluded from coverage by design.
#
# Add a package here only when it is pure logic AND at/above 90% coverage.
#
# internal/subtitles was OUT since #176 added subtitles/auto.go (its auto-search
# orchestrator drives live search/download/persistence) with no unit tests —
# the package fell to 54.4%, dragging the combined floor to 85.4% and blocking
# every push. Follow-up from #188: the package now carries a full unit suite
# (format gating, cascade/refine lifecycle, LinksStore behavior via an
# in-memory sql driver fake) that measures 98%+ WITHOUT a database, matching
# how this gate and PR CI run — so it is back IN.
COVER_PKGS="./internal/version ./internal/stats ./internal/middleware ./internal/contentid ./internal/localstream ./internal/lyrics ./internal/downloader ./internal/jackett ./internal/mailer ./internal/localcache ./internal/musictrending ./internal/transcode ./internal/subtitles"
